## Setup

Bringing up a new {{AGENT_NAME}} agent:

1. **Create the agent** on the DAM platform, granting the connections it needs:
   <!-- TODO(creator): list connections (GitHub, Slack, Telegram, …) and why each. -->
2. **Set the environment variables** — see the table below.
3. **Grab the link to [`ONBOARDING.md`](ONBOARDING.md)** — **from the repo (or fork) you
   actually deploy from**; the agent derives its definition repo from this URL, so a
   fork's agent stays pinned to the fork.
4. **Tell the agent**, in its first message:

   > Here is a file — read it and set yourself up according to it:
   > `https://github.com/<your-org>/{{AGENT_NAME}}/blob/main/ONBOARDING.md`

The agent reads the runbook and, in one pass, checks out its definition, wires up
`work/`, walks you through the configuration dialog, registers the schedules, and marks
itself onboarded.

